# desktop — Agent Instructions

Read `packages/apps/desktop/CLAUDE.md` first. This is the Tauri 2 native shell.

## Key Facts
- Framework: Tauri 2 (Rust) wrapping the built terminal + PyInstaller sidecar
- Runtime file: `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` (sidecar spawn, tray, hotkey, notifications)
- Background runtime: close-to-tray — window close must NOT kill the backend
- Origin: single loopback origin only; no external listeners
- Branch: main (pre-release, all commits to main)

## Working here
- `make desktop-dev` to run; `make desktop-build` for installers
- Rust changes: `cargo check` + `cargo test --lib` in `src-tauri/` before done
- Backend↔shell contracts: ready-port stdout handshake and the
  `FLINTTRADE_NOTIFY\t<title>\t<body>` notification protocol — change both
  sides together (producer `flinttrade_core/desktop_notify.py`)
- Never bundle the Kotak Neo SDK into installers (no redistribution terms)
- Conventional Commits with scope `desktop`

## Verification
Local: cargo check + cargo test --lib green; `make desktop-build` end-to-end
when touching packaging. Cross-OS proof lives in `nightly-cross-platform.yml`
and `desktop-release.yml` (manual) — not per-push CI.
